CAT = "bcgLicensing"; SEG = "LIC"
Q = [
("What is the minimum age for a BC security guard worker licence?",
 "19", ["16", "18", "21"],
 "Section 3 of the Security Services Act sets 19 as the minimum age. The regulation lowers it to 16 only for a few licence types such as alarm monitor, never for security guard."),
("To be licensed as a security worker, an applicant must be ordinarily resident in:",
 "Canada", ["British Columbia", "The city of work", "Canada for five years"],
 "Section 3 requires ordinary residence in Canada, not in BC. A person living in another province can be licensed in BC."),
("A guard holds an Alberta security licence and takes a job in Kelowna. Before working, the guard:",
 "Needs a BC licence", ["May work 90 days", "May work with employer approval", "Needs only a BC address"],
 "The Security Programs Division says a licence from another province does not replace a BC licence. Some provinces' licences make it easier to apply, but a BC licence is still needed."),
("While doing security work, you must carry:",
 "Your physical licence", ["A licence photo", "Your training transcript", "A copy of your application"],
 "Section 8 requires the licence to be carried while working. The Security Programs Division says a photo of the licence is not acceptable."),
("A shopper you have just spoken to on patrol asks to see your licence. You must:",
 "Produce it on request", ["Refuse unless police ask", "Show it at shift end", "Give only your employer's name"],
 "Section 8 requires a licensee to produce the licence on request of anyone to whom they present themselves as a security worker."),
("Which security worker does not have to show the licence to members of the public on request?",
 "A doorperson at a bar", ["A mobile patrol guard on a site", "A shopping mall guard", "A hospital security guard"],
 "Registrar policy exempts armoured car guards and doorpersons at licensed liquor establishments from producing the licence to the public. They must still produce it to inspectors and police."),
("You should hand your physical licence over only to:",
 "Police or special constables", ["Any customer who asks for it", "Your site's property manager", "A bar's liquor server"],
 "You show your licence on request, but the Security Programs Division says to give it only to police officers or special provincial constables."),
("A licensed guard is charged with a criminal offence. The guard must report it to the registrar within:",
 "14 days", ["48 hours", "30 days", "90 days"],
 "Section 9 requires a security worker to report a criminal charge or conviction, or a change of home address, within 14 days."),
("Which change must a licensed guard report to the registrar within 14 days?",
 "A new home address", ["A new shift time", "A new posting site", "A new uniform size"],
 "Section 9 covers a change of residential address and any criminal charge or conviction. Shifts and site postings are matters for the employer."),
("After reporting a new criminal charge, a guard may keep working:",
 "Unless SPD says to stop", ["Only once the case ends", "Only with a police letter", "Only at a non-public post"],
 "The Security Programs Division says a licensee may keep working after reporting unless the Division tells them to stop."),
("A security worker licence is issued for a term of:",
 "3 years", ["1 year", "2 years", "5 years"],
 "Section 6 of the Security Services Regulation sets a three-year term. The security guard under supervision licence is the exception."),
("A security guard under supervision licence lasts:",
 "90 days", ["30 days", "6 months", "1 year"],
 "Section 6(2) of the regulation sets 90 days for the under supervision guard licence, meant for someone completing training or for short events."),
("How many times can one person hold a security guard under supervision licence?",
 "Only once", ["Twice", "Once a year", "Any number of times"],
 "Registrar policy says the guard under supervision licence can be issued to a particular individual only once."),
("At a work site, the ratio of under supervision guards to fully licensed guards must be no more than:",
 "5 to 1", ["2 to 1", "3 to 1", "10 to 1"],
 "Registrar policy 3.6.4 caps the ratio at five under supervision guards for each fully licensed guard at each site."),
("While an under supervision guard is working, a fully licensed guard must be:",
 "Readily available on site", ["Reachable by phone anytime", "On call within the city", "Visiting the site each week"],
 "Policy 3.6.4 requires an unrestricted security guard licensee who can give direct supervision to be readily available at all times at each site."),
("The training standard accepted for a BC security guard licence is:",
 "Basic Security Training", ["Advanced Security Training", "Occupational first aid", "A firearms safety course"],
 "Registrar policy names Basic Security Training (or the older Basic Standard Training Levels 1 and 2) as the standard. Advanced Security Training is the extra course for restraint authorization."),
("A former police officer with general duty experience applies for a guard licence. The officer:",
 "May apply without taking BST", ["Must take BST twice", "Needs no licence at all", "Must keep a police appointment"],
 "Policy 2.6.6.2 lets people with general duty experience as police, corrections, sheriff, auxiliary, reserve or border officers apply directly. They still need a licence."),
("A security guard must be fluent enough in English to:",
 "Converse with the public", ["Write in two languages", "Pass a written essay", "Teach the training course"],
 "The regulation requires sufficient English fluency to converse with the public while working. Policy sets the minimum at Canadian Language Benchmark 5 for listening and speaking."),
("A friend with no licence asks to borrow yours for one shift. Under the Act, a licence:",
 "Can't be lent or transferred", ["May be lent to a trainee", "May be lent with notice", "May be shared within a company"],
 "Section 7 says a worker licence is not transferable and must not be used by anyone else."),
("Your licence expired yesterday and your renewal is not approved yet. You:",
 "Must not work as a guard", ["May work for 30 days", "May work with a copy", "May work under supervision"],
 "The Security Programs Division says not to do security work with an expired licence. An under supervision licence is a separate licence, not a grace period."),
("On the chest of a security guard's shirt, the word SECURITY must be in letters at least:",
 "1.25 cm high", ["2.5 cm high", "5 cm high", "7.5 cm high"],
 "Section 12 of the regulation sets at least 1.25 cm on the chest. The back of an outer garment needs letters at least 5 cm high."),
("Besides the word SECURITY, a guard's uniform must display:",
 "The employer's name", ["The guard's home address", "The licence number", "A police-style crest"],
 "Section 12 requires the name of the person who employed or engaged the licensee. Police-style uniforms are prohibited."),
("Which item is a BC security guard not allowed to carry?",
 "An ID badge", ["A notebook", "A flashlight with batteries", "A two-way radio"],
 "Section 12(3) of the regulation bars licensees from carrying or using an identification badge, which could be mistaken for a police badge."),
("A belt with an over-the-shoulder strap linked to the waist belt is:",
 "Prohibited for guards", ["Required on patrols", "Allowed with approval", "Allowed for supervisors"],
 "Section 12(3) bans the Sam Browne style strap linked to a waist belt, because it resembles police equipment."),
("A security company advertises its guards as \"private police\". Under the Act this is:",
 "An offence under the Act", ["Allowed if licensed", "Allowed with registrar approval", "Only a customer complaint"],
 "Section 44(5) prohibits using the words detective, law enforcement, peace officer or police to describe security work or a security business."),
("A security patrol vehicle must show the word SECURITY on both sides in letters at least:",
 "7.5 cm high", ["5 cm high", "10 cm high", "15 cm high"],
 "Section 10(4) of the regulation sets 7.5 cm letters on both sides, plus the employer's name and telephone number."),
("A guard patrol vehicle may use flashing lights that are:",
 "Amber, at the contract site", ["Red, at any time of day", "Blue, while going to alarms", "Amber, to clear traffic"],
 "Policy 3.7.5 allows only flashing amber lights, only while doing security work at a contract site, and never for right of way."),
("Which use of a guard patrol vehicle is prohibited?",
 "Holding an arrested person", ["Patrolling a parking lot", "Carrying a first aid kit", "Using a white search light"],
 "Policy 3.7.7 bars using a patrol vehicle to hold or transport someone detained or arrested before police arrive. One white search light is allowed."),
("Which equipment may a guard patrol vehicle have?",
 "One white search light", ["A siren or loudspeaker", "A rear seat prisoner cage", "A police crash bumper"],
 "Policy 3.7.7 allows one vehicle-mounted white search light and bans sirens, prisoner cages and police-style crash bumpers."),
("A self-employed guard who contracts directly with clients needs:",
 "Both kinds of licence", ["Only a worker licence", "Only a business licence", "A peace officer appointment"],
 "The Security Programs Division says self-employed contractors need a security worker licence and a security business licence."),
("Which licensed security workers may be authorized to carry firearms on duty?",
 "Armoured car guards only", ["Mobile patrol guards", "Door staff at bars", "Loss prevention officers"],
 "Section 26 of the Act bans firearms in security work, except that the registrar may allow armoured car guards who meet the requirements."),
("An unpaid volunteer doing door security at a licensed bar:",
 "Needs a guard licence", ["Needs no licence at all", "Needs only a server permit", "Needs only basic training"],
 "The regulation exempts most unpaid security work, but not door security at a liquor-licensed establishment."),
]
